# Learner reflections with the published answer-order contribution

This is the receiving successor to the
[original main qualification](original-main/README.md). It composes the
reflection notebook with the exact published
[answer-order PR #12](https://github.com/Jacob-Met/RecallWeave/pull/12), head
`e68ac2f97fe89f74e7b39256db0778a4b98c6dad` on
`work/answer-order-a3425ebf9874`. The common original main is
`3e3217959bdf277ae5ef61a7afe68142e2626486`.

## What the learner can do

After completing the lesson, write and revise an explanation beside each
question's existing transfer prompt, including questions answered correctly.
The final Apply-it prompt has its own response field. Writing stays attached
to canonical question IDs during review and practice navigation and is
included in the actual study-notes download as unscored learner text. Clearing
a field clears that note; a fresh local session clears the notebook through
the existing reload. First answers, practice outcomes and model estimates
remain separate from the writing.

The change uses the existing native JavaScript modules and standalone builder.
It adds no account, automatic storage, upload, model call, sync, trace format
or course content. The application prompt retains the exact original bundled
course wording. The imported-deck and completed-trace restore owners retain
their separate receiving responsibilities, described below.

## Exact composition

The reflection module and exporter are byte-identical to their independently
reviewed original-main source. The only shared merge resolutions keep both
independent imports in `app.mjs` and include both modules in the existing
single-file builder. The owner's answer-order helper, tests and browser
drivers remain exact PR #12 bytes. Its `renderQuestion`, `submitAnswer` and
`renderPracticeQuestion` functions are also preserved byte for byte.

The owner keeps one per-question permutation for the session and uses original
option indices for correctness and review. The reflection notebook uses the
question ID, so changing option presentation does not change note association.
The source deck, knowledge model and review/practice module retain their
original bytes.

